{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","statement":"Hybrid Code Networks (HCNs) combine a recurrent neural network with domain-specific knowledge encoded as software and system action templates.","source_span":"we introduce Hybrid Code Networks (HCNs), which combine an RNN with domain-specific knowledge encoded as software and system action templates"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","statement":"HCNs attain state-of-the-art performance on the bAbI dialog dataset and outperform two commercially deployed customer-facing dialog systems.","source_span":"HCNs attain state-of-the-art performance on the bAbI dialog dataset, and outperform two commercially deployed customer-facing dialog systems."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","statement":"HCNs can be optimized with supervised learning, reinforcement learning, or a mixture of both.","source_span":"HCNs can be optimized with supervised learning, reinforcement learning, or a mixture of both."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","statement":"The four components of a Hybrid Code Network are a recurrent neural network, domain-specific software, domain-specific action templates, and a conventional entity extraction module for identifying entity mentions in text.","source_span":"the four components of a Hybrid Code Network are a recurrent neural network; domain-specific software; domain-specific action templates; and a conventional entity extraction module for identifying entity mentions in text"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","statement":"The RNN used in the HCN model can be a long short-term memory (LSTM) or a gated recurrent unit (GRU).","source_span":"This vector is passed to an RNN, such as a long short-term memory (LSTM) BIBREF1 or gated recurrent unit (GRU) BIBREF2 ."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","statement":"Entity tracking code can optionally return an 'action mask' as a bit vector indicating which actions are permitted at the current timestep.","source_span":"This code can optionally return an \u201caction mask\u201d, indicating actions which are permitted at the current timestep, as a bit vector."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","statement":"The dense layer with softmax activation in the HCN has an output dimension equal to the number of distinct system action templates, producing a distribution over action templates.","source_span":"passed to a dense layer with a softmax activation, with output dimension equal to the number of distinct system action templates"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","statement":"When reinforcement learning is active, an action is sampled from the probability distribution for exploration; when RL is not active, the action with the highest probability is always selected.","source_span":"when RL is active, exploration is required, so in this case an action is sampled from the distribution; when RL is not active, the best action should be chosen, and so the action with the highest probability is always selected"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","statement":"The paper gives the example that a banking dialog system would require a user to be logged in before they can retrieve account information, illustrating the need for programmed constraints.","source_span":"a banking dialog system would require that a user is logged in before they can retrieve account information"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","statement":"Traditional pipeline-based dialog systems include modules for language understanding, dialog state tracking, action selection policy, and language generation.","source_span":"The first decomposes a dialog system into a pipeline, typically including language understanding, dialog state tracking, action selection policy, and language generation"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","statement":"\"Entity output\" developer code substitutes entities into the selected action template to produce a fully-formed action, for example mapping the template \"<city>, right?\" to \"Seattle, right?\".","source_span":"mapping the template \u201c<city>, right?\u201d to \u201cSeattle, right?\u201d"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What are the four components that make up a Hybrid Code Network?","answer":"A Hybrid Code Network consists of a recurrent neural network, domain-specific software, domain-specific action templates, and a conventional entity extraction module for identifying entity mentions in text."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What learning methods can be used to optimize Hybrid Code Networks?","answer":"HCNs can be optimized with supervised learning, reinforcement learning, or a mixture of both."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","fact_refs":[1],"question":"On what dataset do HCNs achieve state-of-the-art performance, and what other systems do they outperform?","answer":"HCNs attain state-of-the-art performance on the bAbI dialog dataset and outperform two commercially deployed customer-facing dialog systems."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What types of recurrent neural network cells does the HCN model support?","answer":"The HCN model's RNN can be implemented as a long short-term memory (LSTM) or a gated recurrent unit (GRU)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What is the purpose of the 'action mask' returned by the entity tracking code in an HCN?","answer":"The action mask is a bit vector, optionally returned by the entity tracking code, that indicates which actions are permitted at the current timestep."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","fact_refs":[8],"question":"What example does the paper use to illustrate why programmed constraints are essential in some dialog systems?","answer":"The paper notes that a banking dialog system would require that a user is logged in before they can retrieve account information."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0130","fact_refs":[7],"question":"How does an HCN choose an action differently when reinforcement learning is active versus inactive?","answer":"When RL is active, an action is sampled from the probability distribution to allow exploration; when RL is not active, the action with the highest probability is always selected."}
